# Theming Rules

## Startup order (Application.Styles)

```xml
<my:MyTheme />
<my:ThemeControlsCatalog />
<!-- then Extended, Geography, app-specific styles -->
```

Call `MyTheme.Current.EnsureLoaded()` at app initialization.

## ControlTheme conventions

- Implicit key: `x:Key="{x:Type my:Control}"` or `{x:Type Button}`
- Named variant: `MyNet.Theme.{Control}.{Variant}`
- Template resource keys: `MyNet.{Control}.Template.{Variant}`
- One file per control: `{ControlName}.axaml`

## Resource keys

Prefix all tokens with `MyNet.*` (e.g. `MyNet.Color.Surface.Level1`, `MyNet.Font.Size.H5`).

## Layers in ThemeControlsCatalog

Foundation → Standard → Custom → Presets → Resources

## Assists

- Theme assists: `MyNet.Avalonia.Theme/Assists/` (`VariantAssist`, `ShadowAssist`, …)
- Control assists: `MyNet.Avalonia.Theme.Controls/Assists/` (`IconAssist`, `DataGridAssist`, …)

## CSS utility classes

Use `CssClass` registries (`variant-*`, `size-*`, `kind-*`) — not ad-hoc class strings.

Visual customization must not require subclassing controls.
